{"title": "Hello Weather is the best Apple Weather app on Android", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/hello-weather-android-apple/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/Hello-Weather-cover.jpg?quality=82&strip=all&w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While Pixel Weather serves my needs quite well, I’ve been looking for a way to check Apple Weather (previously Dark Sky) forecast data on Android, and I’ve finally found it with <a href=\"https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.helloweatherapp\">Hello Weather by Electric Dream Machine</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/hello-weather-android-apple/#more-740363\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-25T09:44:03+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-25T19:52:14.284119+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
{"title": "Save serious money with RedPocket Mobile’s $5 Black Friday plans", "link": "https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/save-serious-money-with-redpockets-black-friday-plans-that-start-at-5-a-month-sponsored/", "summary": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5google.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/4/2026/11/00947cc8ee4c3fe022e46888fd9a63f8_abt-us-mob.webp?w=1536\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You’re not going to believe this, but there’s one part of your life that’s not actually getting more expensive. If you <a href=\"https://www.redpocket.com/shop?utm_source=9to5&utm_medium=referral&utm_campaign=9to5_article\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow\">switch to RedPocket Mobile</a> during its Black Friday sale, you can ditch your costly carrier and get a plan that starts at $5 per month. It’s not too good to be true: RedPocket has been around for 20 years, and unlike most MVNOs, it’s independently owned and operated. That gives it the ability to offer you real network choice when you sign up for a new plan (we’ll explain more later), and keeps your costs low. Really low.</p>\n\n\n\n <a class=\"more-link\" href=\"https://9to5google.com/2026/11/25/save-serious-money-with-redpockets-black-friday-plans-that-start-at-5-a-month-sponsored/#more-735678\">more…</a>", "published": "2026-11-25T08:41:47+00:00", "source": "9to5Google", "category": "subscription", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-11-25T19:52:14.284119+00:00", "ontology": {"repo": "SubscriptionRadar", "category": "subscription", "ontology_version": "0.1.0", "evidence_policy_ids": ["traceable_url_required", "cross_reference_required", "non_authoritative_context_only"]}}
